# Example environment file. Copy to ``.env`` and customise.
#
# The runtime currently reads NO environment variables; everything is
# driven through ``config/settings.yaml`` and ``config/minecraft.yaml``.
# This file exists as a stub so that when future features need env-only
# secrets (API keys for an LLM teacher, telemetry endpoints, etc.) the
# convention is already in place.
#
# Anything you add here should also be loaded explicitly in code via
# ``os.environ.get("NAME", default)`` — we do NOT auto-import .env at
# startup. Add ``python-dotenv`` to requirements.txt and a single
# ``load_dotenv()`` call near the top of ``main.py`` if/when that
# changes.

# Example (commented out):
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# WANDB_API_KEY=
# CLAUDE_API_KEY=
